  "details": "Option to separate Voice, World, and Avatar sounds for playback on different devices.\n\nThis would be an option for advanced users, allowing offloading of audio mixing to external processes, allowing them to leverage more complicated audio mastering and processing techniques.\n\nThe examples that come to mind include ducking world audio when people are talking, or for people with physical mixers being able to quickly and intuitively mute avatar sounds if someone has obnoxious avatar effects.\n\nI realize this might be a bit of an edge case, but would be a boon for content creators using VRC.",
